  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "Orthodontic Impression Techniques: Traditional vs. Digital"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Ensuring Accuracy for Effective Treatment"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Accurate dental impressions are fundamental in orthodontics, serving as the blueprint for effective treatment plans. In this article, we’ll explore both traditional and modern impression techniques and explain why accuracy is crucial for successful treatment."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Traditional Impression Techniques in Orthodontics"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Traditional methods involve using alginate or polyvinyl siloxane materials to create molds of the patient’s teeth and gums. These materials are placed in trays, inserted into the patient’s mouth, and held in place until they set. While effective, this method can be uncomfortable for patients and prone to minor inaccuracies due to movement during the setting process."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The Rise of Digital Impressions"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Advancements in technology have introduced digital impression techniques, offering greater precision and comfort. Intraoral scanners, like the iTero, capture detailed images of the teeth and gums, creating a digital 3D model. This method eliminates the need for physical molds, reduces patient discomfort, and minimizes errors. These digital models can be easily shared with dental labs to produce appliances like braces, aligners, and retainers."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Why Accuracy Matters in Orthodontic Impressions"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Ensuring accuracy in impressions is crucial for the success of orthodontic treatment. Inaccurate impressions can lead to poorly fitting appliances, extended treatment time, and discomfort. On the other hand, accurate impressions help ensure appliances fit properly, promoting effective tooth movement and timely results."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Our Commitment to Precision at Dr. Dante Gonzales’ Office"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "At Dr. Dante Gonzales’ office, we prioritize precision in every aspect of our orthodontic care. Our team utilizes the latest digital scanning technology to ensure the highest accuracy and patient comfort. By integrating these advanced techniques, we provide personalized treatment plans that deliver optimal results — helping our patients achieve their perfect smiles efficiently and comfortably."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Learn more about our orthodontic services or schedule a consultation today."
    }
  ],
